.TH FORGE 1 "2026" "forge 0.1.0" "Forge Manual"
.SH NAME
forge \- a terminal text editor in the classic keyboard-driven tradition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forge
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Forge is a modal-capable terminal editor: keys run named commands, help is built from the same structured documentation that this page is, and the manual can be read in the editor with \fIC\-h i\fR. Files named on the command line are visited in order; \fB+LINE[:COLUMN]\fR may precede a file name to move point into it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-no-config
don't run ~/.config/forge/init.rhai
.TP
.B \-\-chdir \fIDIR\fR
change to DIR before opening files
.TP
.B \-\-file \fIFILE\fR
visit FILE (same as a positional file name)
.TP
.B \-\-find-file \fIFILE\fR
visit FILE (same as a positional file name)
.TP
.B \-\-visit \fIFILE\fR
visit FILE (same as a positional file name)
.TP
.B +LINE[:COLUMN]
go to LINE (and optional zero-based COLUMN) in the next file
.TP
.B \-\-plugin \fIFILE\fR
load a plugin (a .wasm component); may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-check-plugin \fIFILE\fR
load a plugin without the editor, show what it set up, run its commands (answering questions with \-\-answer), open files, wait for events and its processes' output
.TP
.B \-\-headless
run the editor without a terminal and print the screen (for testing plugins end to end)
.TP
.B \-\-package-entry \fIFILE.wasm\fR
print a package index entry for a plugin (see docs/plugin-api.md, "Sharing plugins")
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show the help
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
show the version
.SH SEE ALSO
The Forge manual: press \fIC\-h i\fR in the editor, or open \fImanual.html\fR on the documentation site. The \fBforge\fR plugin API is documented in \fIplugin-api.md\fR.
